    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0139" n="35" xml:id="pg35"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 20,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Blaine instructs Mr. Mizner promptly to demand of the Guatemalan Government
                    the instant surrender of the <hi rendition="#italic">Colima</hi>, with all her
                    cargo, that Government having no right whatever to detain her, as she had been
                    guilty of no offense against any treaty existing or against the law of
                    nations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
